{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792531083719,"sessionID":"ses_ea4d262f1ffeH3oB1ZEnAed0SK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_lDEUHjWaVeVeZuOi9LLs3068","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\40-critique.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\40-critique.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Critique — 2026-10-20\n2: \n3: The critic cannot take image input (the model returns an error on the stills), so\n4: this is judged the same way the builder did: `report.json` exit codes and degraded\n5: flags, `node tools/check-registry.mjs --json`, the rendered `square.output.json`\n6: (feasible, 25 sources, no warnings), the flattened layout, and a line-by-line read\n7: of `src/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1/*.ts` and its test. The milestone\n8: ladder was re-checked against Project-GC's Milestones tab verbatim: \"1, 10, 50 and\n9: 100 ... up to 1000 every hundredth ... between 1000 and 5000 every five hundredth\n10: ... beyond that every thousandth\" — `isMilestone` matches it exactly, including\n11: the 1000 boundary (hundreds tier) and 1500 (five-hundreds tier).\n12: \n13: ## Scores\n14: \n15: | variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n16: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n17: | a | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16 | no |\n18: | b | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16 | no |\n19: \n20: ## What each variant gets right / wrong\n21: \n22: **a (in place).** Right: the one concept is real and correct — `isMilestone` /\n23: `ordinal` are pure, exported, unit-tested, and match Project-GC exactly, so the\n24: \"1,000th find\" + MILESTONE badge cannot disagree with the typed 1,000. Fail-fast\n25: is genuinely adversarial (misspelled type with a did-you-mean, mix that sums past\n26: findCount, non-integer findCount, unknown prop) and the test asserts the actual\n27: messages. The layout contract is not a widened ruler — header top band, full-width\n28: mix bar, three `equal: \"size\"` tiles, footer band, square badge all name what the\n29: brief promised, and the default mix sums to exactly 1000 (no grey Other).\n30: \n31: Wrong / weak: the why-tutorial's `timeline` still lists only scout (x3) + plan —\n32: the build phase (109 calls, $0.99 in `trace.json`) is missing, so `tutorial-6`\n33: \"how it was made\" under-reports the run; that is a ship-phase re-mint\n34: (`node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline`), not a blocker. The brief's props table\n35: says \"8 + debugLayout\" but the template ships a 9th data prop (`footer`), which the\n36: brief's layout section describes but the table omits — harmless, mildly untidy.\n37: The value angle is the honest weak spot (line 6): the scouted artifact is the My\n38: Finds GPX, but the card retypes numbers instead of importing, and Project-GC /\n39: CacheSleuth already surface the milestone — only the clean deterministic share card\n40: differentiates it, and the caveats say so.\n41: \n42: **b (night-cache preset).** Its `src` snapshot carries the `preset` knob (37 KB vs\n43: 36 KB), but it was reverted and its `report.json` + stills are byte-identical to a\n44: (the light default); the only evidence of the idea is\n45: `variants/b/renders/dark.png`. It adds nothing distinct over a at defaults, so it\n46: is judged the same and contributes no reason to prefer it.\n47: \n48: ## Decision: SHIP a\n49: \n50: No fatal. No degraded render (exit 0 on all three canvases, `check-registry`\n51: renders all 35 with zero errors/warnings on this template), every prop has a\n52: default, the pack/slug describe it, the problem page cites only sources the scout\n53: actually opened, and the solution page claims only what the variant does.\n54: \n55: ## What a human polish pass should look at first\n56: \n57: 1. The why-tutorial timeline (ship phase re-mints it — make sure build lands in\n58:    `WHY.timeline` before `npm run verify`).\n59: 2. `footer` is an undocumented 9th prop in the brief's \"8 + debugLayout\" table —\n60:    add it to the brief or drop it, so the count matches.\n61: 3. Visual cramping at 640x360 / 480x270: the contract proves text fits, but a\n62:    human eye on the legend line and the badge at the floor is the one thing the\n63:    builder could not do.\n\n(End of file - total 63 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Critique — 2026-10-20\n\nThe critic cannot take image input (the model returns an error on the stills), so\nthis is judged the same way the builder did: `report.json` exit codes and degraded\nflags, `node tools/check-registry.mjs --json`, the rendered `square.output.json`\n(feasible, 25 sources, no warnings), the flattened layout, and a line-by-line read\nof `src/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1/*.ts` and its test. The milestone\nladder was re-checked against Project-GC's Milestones tab verbatim: \"1, 10, 50 and\n100 ... up to 1000 every hundredth ... between 1000 and 5000 every five hundredth\n... beyond that every thousandth\" — `isMilestone` matches it exactly, including\nthe 1000 boundary (hundreds tier) and 1500 (five-hundreds tier).\n\n## Scores\n\n| variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16 | no |\n| b | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16 | no |\n\n## What each variant gets right / wrong","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\40-critique.md","text":"# Critique — 2026-10-20\n\nThe critic cannot take image input (the model returns an error on the stills), so\nthis is judged the same way the builder did: `report.json` exit codes and degraded\nflags, `node tools/check-registry.mjs --json`, the rendered `square.output.json`\n(feasible, 25 sources, no warnings), the flattened layout, and a line-by-line read\nof `src/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1/*.ts` and its test. The milestone\nladder was re-checked against Project-GC's Milestones tab verbatim: \"1, 10, 50 and\n100 ... up to 1000 every hundredth ... between 1000 and 5000 every five hundredth\n... beyond that every thousandth\" — `isMilestone` matches it exactly, including\nthe 1000 boundary (hundreds tier) and 1500 (five-hundreds tier).\n\n## Scores\n\n| variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| a | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16 | no |\n| b | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16 | no |\n\n## What each variant gets right / wrong\n\n**a (in place).** Right: the one concept is real and correct — `isMilestone` /\n`ordinal` are pure, exported, unit-tested, and match Project-GC exactly, so the\n\"1,000th find\" + MILESTONE badge cannot disagree with the typed 1,000. Fail-fast\nis genuinely adversarial (misspelled type with a did-you-mean, mix that sums past\nfindCount, non-integer findCount, unknown prop) and the test asserts the actual\nmessages. The layout contract is not a widened ruler — header top band, full-width\nmix bar, three `equal: \"size\"` tiles, footer band, square badge all name what the\nbrief promised, and the default mix sums to exactly 1000 (no grey Other).\n\nWrong / weak: the why-tutorial's `timeline` still lists only scout (x3) + plan —\nthe build phase (109 calls, $0.99 in `trace.json`) is missing, so `tutorial-6`\n\"how it was made\" under-reports the run; that is a ship-phase re-mint\n(`node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline`), not a blocker. The brief's props table\nsays \"8 + debugLayout\" but the template ships a 9th data prop (`footer`), which the\nbrief's layout section describes but the table omits — harmless, mildly untidy.\nThe value angle is the honest weak spot (line 6): the scouted artifact is the My\nFinds GPX, but the card retypes numbers instead of importing, and Project-GC /\nCacheSleuth already surface the milestone — only the clean deterministic share card\ndifferentiates it, and the caveats say so.\n\n**b (night-cache preset).** Its `src` snapshot carries the `preset` knob (37 KB vs\n36 KB), but it was reverted and its `report.json` + stills are byte-identical to a\n(the light default); the only evidence of the idea is\n`variants/b/renders/dark.png`. It adds nothing distinct over a at defaults, so it\nis judged the same and contributes no reason to prefer it.\n\n## Decision: SHIP a\n\nNo fatal. No degraded render (exit 0 on all three canvases, `check-registry`\nrenders all 35 with zero errors/warnings on this template), every prop has a\ndefault, the pack/slug describe it, the problem page cites only sources the scout\nactually opened, and the solution page claims only what the variant does.\n\n## What a human polish pass should look at first\n\n1. The why-tutorial timeline (ship phase re-mints it — make sure build lands in\n   `WHY.timeline` before `npm run verify`).\n2. `footer` is an undocumented 9th prop in the brief's \"8 + debugLayout\" table —\n   add it to the brief or drop it, so the count matches.\n3. Visual cramping at 640x360 / 480x270: the contract proves text fits, but a\n   human eye on the legend line and the badge at the floor is the one thing the\n   builder could not do.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":63,"totalLines":63,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-20\\40-critique.md","time":{"start":1792531083704,"end":1792531083717}},"id":"prt_15b2db1050017UZpioY4x8VvV7","sessionID":"ses_ea4d262f1ffeH3oB1ZEnAed0SK","messageID":"msg_15b2d9f03001zBNEF9zvyDdhQd"}}
