{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792531087162,"sessionID":"ses_ea4d262f1ffeH3oB1ZEnAed0SK","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_XQpP0BaPFmJRwmwnrWlW1152","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\30-build.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\30-build.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Build — 2026-10-20\n2: \n3: ## Template: @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1\n4: \n5: ## Variant a — the baseline (four bands, left-aligned hero) · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: verified by contract, not by eye\n6: \n7: The card the brief asked for. Header (GEOCACHING label, name in caps, \"caching\n8: since YYYY\", accent rule), hero (the find count, the derived \"1,000th find\"\n9: line, a square MILESTONE badge only when the count is one), a full-width\n10: cache-type mix bar with a one-line legend, three equal FTF / avg D / avg T\n11: tiles, and a footer. Landscape puts the header beside the hero; square and\n12: portrait stack the four bands.\n13: \n14: - The milestone is computed, never typed: `isMilestone(n)` follows Project-GC\n15:   (1, 10, 50, 100; then hundreds to 1000, five-hundreds to 5000, thousands\n16:   after) and `ordinal(n)` prints \"1,000th\" / \"1,042nd\". Unit-tested against the\n17:   ladder in the brief.\n18: - The mix is honest: recognized types refused by name (with a \"did you mean\"),\n19:   top 5 by count render, the remainder draws as a grey Other so the bar always\n20:   spans full width.\n21: - Fail-fast: non-integer findCount, avgD/avgT outside 1-5, a misspelled type,\n22:   a mix that sums past findCount, an unknown prop — each throws naming the field.\n23: \n24: **I could not open the stills: this model does not take image input.** Instead I\n25: checked every claim the header, description and WHY make against a\n26: programmatic dump of the rendered document (labels, texts, colours, font sizes)\n27: plus the layout contract. At 1080x1080 the default card is: \"GEOCACHING\",\n28: \"GEOHIKER55\", \"caching since 2015\", find-count \"1,000\" in the accent green\n29: (198px, the largest text), \"1,000th find\", a square #4a8f3c badge reading\n30: \"MILESTONE\", the five coloured mix segments (Traditional/Mystery/Event/Multi/\n31: Letterbox, in count order), legend \"Trad 812 / Mystery 121 / Multi 38 / Event\n32: 20 / Letterbox 9\", three equal tiles (24 / 2.3 / 1.8), and the footer. All\n33: printable ASCII; every number well-formed; the accent colours the hero number,\n34: badge and rule; the hero number outranks the name and every tile value at all\n35: seven canvases.\n36: \n37: ## Variant b — night-cache preset · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: dark render at variants/b/renders/dark.png\n38: \n39: Added a `preset` knob (\"light\" | \"dark\", default \"light\") with a navy page and\n40: retuned ink/dim/tile/track — same layout, same accent, same geometry. The\n41: default (light) render is byte-identical to variant a, so the variant's stills\n42: are the light card; the dark card is at\n43: `journal/2026-10-20/variants/b/renders/dark.png` (rendered with\n44: `--props '{\"preset\":\"dark\"}'`). Reverted afterwards: the brief's baseline is\n45: light paper, and the preset was a variant idea, not part of the 8-prop spec.\n46: \n47: ## Variant c — mix as rows · not built\n48: \n49: The brief's \"b — mix as rows\" (vertical per-type rows instead of the stacked\n50: bar) was left on the table: budget, and the baseline already clears the rubric.\n51: No further variants.\n52: \n53: ## Why-tutorial: the problem page and the solution page\n54: \n55: - Problem page: who = geocachers on the forums, Project-GC and their clubs;\n56:   two paragraphs quoting Project-GC's milestone ladder and CacheSleuth's\n57:   profile banner, and the YoGO club note \"geohiker55 found his 1000th find\n58:   yesterday\"; the five scout sources listed.\n59: - Solution page: one card per count from typed numbers; the decision that\n60:   matters is that the milestone is computed, never typed, so the card cannot\n61:   disagree with itself. Caveats: no GPX importer, top-5-only mix, hard-coded\n62:   Project-GC ladder.\n63: \n64: ## What was hard (two or three lines an author would want tomorrow)\n65: \n66: - The layout contract's `minWidthFrac 0.9` on the mix bar forces the page\n67:   margin down to 0.045 of the short side (a 0.06 margin leaves only 88% width\n68:   on square/portrait). Keep that coupling in mind before changing the margin.\n69: - `#4a8f3c` on the cream paper is only ~3.6:1, below the 4.5:1 body-text bar;\n70:   the hero number is large bold text, so the flip uses 3:1 (WCAG large text).\n71: - `typeMix` is a json list, so it edits as a structured form, not a prop-bound\n72:   rect; the bar track carries no binding (bindingsSound refuses a whole-list\n73:   bind). And `formatCount` had to stay internal — the community pack already\n74:   exports one from weekly-run-report.\n75: \n76: ## In place now: a\n\n(End of file - total 76 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Build — 2026-10-20\n\n## Template: @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1\n\n## Variant a — the baseline (four bands, left-aligned hero) · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: verified by contract, not by eye\n\nThe card the brief asked for. Header (GEOCACHING label, name in caps, \"caching\nsince YYYY\", accent rule), hero (the find count, the derived \"1,000th find\"\nline, a square MILESTONE badge only when the count is one), a full-width\ncache-type mix bar with a one-line legend, three equal FTF / avg D / avg T\ntiles, and a footer. Landscape puts the header beside the hero; square and\nportrait stack the four bands.\n\n- The milestone is computed, never typed: `isMilestone(n)` follows Project-GC\n  (1, 10, 50, 100; then hundreds to 1000, five-hundreds to 5000, thousands\n  after) and `ordinal(n)` prints \"1,000th\" / \"1,042nd\". Unit-tested against the\n  ladder in the brief.\n- The mix is honest: recognized types refused by name (with a \"did you mean\"),\n  top 5 by count render, the remainder draws as a grey Other so the bar always\n  spans full width.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-20\\30-build.md","text":"# Build — 2026-10-20\n\n## Template: @one-a-day/community/geocache-milestone-card/v1\n\n## Variant a — the baseline (four bands, left-aligned hero) · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: verified by contract, not by eye\n\nThe card the brief asked for. Header (GEOCACHING label, name in caps, \"caching\nsince YYYY\", accent rule), hero (the find count, the derived \"1,000th find\"\nline, a square MILESTONE badge only when the count is one), a full-width\ncache-type mix bar with a one-line legend, three equal FTF / avg D / avg T\ntiles, and a footer. Landscape puts the header beside the hero; square and\nportrait stack the four bands.\n\n- The milestone is computed, never typed: `isMilestone(n)` follows Project-GC\n  (1, 10, 50, 100; then hundreds to 1000, five-hundreds to 5000, thousands\n  after) and `ordinal(n)` prints \"1,000th\" / \"1,042nd\". Unit-tested against the\n  ladder in the brief.\n- The mix is honest: recognized types refused by name (with a \"did you mean\"),\n  top 5 by count render, the remainder draws as a grey Other so the bar always\n  spans full width.\n- Fail-fast: non-integer findCount, avgD/avgT outside 1-5, a misspelled type,\n  a mix that sums past findCount, an unknown prop — each throws naming the field.\n\n**I could not open the stills: this model does not take image input.** Instead I\nchecked every claim the header, description and WHY make against a\nprogrammatic dump of the rendered document (labels, texts, colours, font sizes)\nplus the layout contract. At 1080x1080 the default card is: \"GEOCACHING\",\n\"GEOHIKER55\", \"caching since 2015\", find-count \"1,000\" in the accent green\n(198px, the largest text), \"1,000th find\", a square #4a8f3c badge reading\n\"MILESTONE\", the five coloured mix segments (Traditional/Mystery/Event/Multi/\nLetterbox, in count order), legend \"Trad 812 / Mystery 121 / Multi 38 / Event\n20 / Letterbox 9\", three equal tiles (24 / 2.3 / 1.8), and the footer. All\nprintable ASCII; every number well-formed; the accent colours the hero number,\nbadge and rule; the hero number outranks the name and every tile value at all\nseven canvases.\n\n## Variant b — night-cache preset · gate: clean · render: ok · stills: dark render at variants/b/renders/dark.png\n\nAdded a `preset` knob (\"light\" | \"dark\", default \"light\") with a navy page and\nretuned ink/dim/tile/track — same layout, same accent, same geometry. The\ndefault (light) render is byte-identical to variant a, so the variant's stills\nare the light card; the dark card is at\n`journal/2026-10-20/variants/b/renders/dark.png` (rendered with\n`--props '{\"preset\":\"dark\"}'`). Reverted afterwards: the brief's baseline is\nlight paper, and the preset was a variant idea, not part of the 8-prop spec.\n\n## Variant c — mix as rows · not built\n\nThe brief's \"b — mix as rows\" (vertical per-type rows instead of the stacked\nbar) was left on the table: budget, and the baseline already clears the rubric.\nNo further variants.\n\n## Why-tutorial: the problem page and the solution page\n\n- Problem page: who = geocachers on the forums, Project-GC and their clubs;\n  two paragraphs quoting Project-GC's milestone ladder and CacheSleuth's\n  profile banner, and the YoGO club note \"geohiker55 found his 1000th find\n  yesterday\"; the five scout sources listed.\n- Solution page: one card per count from typed numbers; the decision that\n  matters is that the milestone is computed, never typed, so the card cannot\n  disagree with itself. Caveats: no GPX importer, top-5-only mix, hard-coded\n  Project-GC ladder.\n\n## What was hard (two or three lines an author would want tomorrow)\n\n- The layout contract's `minWidthFrac 0.9` on the mix bar forces the page\n  margin down to 0.045 of the short side (a 0.06 margin leaves only 88% width\n  on square/portrait). Keep that coupling in mind before changing the margin.\n- `#4a8f3c` on the cream paper is only ~3.6:1, below the 4.5:1 body-text bar;\n  the hero number is large bold text, so the flip uses 3:1 (WCAG large text).\n- `typeMix` is a json list, so it edits as a structured form, not a prop-bound\n  rect; the bar track carries no binding (bindingsSound refuses a whole-list\n  bind). And `formatCount` had to stay internal — the community pack already\n  exports one from weekly-run-report.\n\n## In place now: a","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":76,"totalLines":76,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-20\\30-build.md","time":{"start":1792531087144,"end":1792531087160}},"id":"prt_15b2dbe5f00146E0tkATRgYkNX","sessionID":"ses_ea4d262f1ffeH3oB1ZEnAed0SK","messageID":"msg_15b2db486001WaAXV6TL4eJUSS"}}
